{"id": "q0033", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 425375537, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "Dominick went to his team's changing room and saw half as many robots as helmets and half as many helmets as footballs kept there. If there were 20 helmets, calculate the total number of items Dominick saw.\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0033.wav", "input_sha256": "c164aa67533d3436c71dbb71b12554e38945f5cdb8aa47bd1a8c9c0f79cf92e8", "input_samples": 265800, "input_s": 16.613, "n_real_chunks": 17, "score": 0.3349, "act": 0.9945, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So let's break this down. If there are 2 0 helmets, and the number of robots is half as many as helmets, then there are 10 robots. And since helmet s are half as many as footballs, that means there are 40 football s. Add ing them all together—2 0 helmet s plus 10 robot s plus 40 football s gives us a total of 70 items.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 16, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 23, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0033_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "71698231631a3d290213cc9df60c4fe9d4eeca00e374a2c3cfc76500b3552012", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 23.24}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.078, 1.141, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.081, 2.144, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.081, 3.143, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.077